473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (Ticket sales make up the vast majority of NorthByte's revenue. Fares vary by route, distance, and season, with demand peaking during the summer months and the December holidays. Passengers travelling between two cities without a direct NorthByte flight can connect through one of NorthByte's hubs; in that case, a single booking includes two or more flights, and each flight is recorded as its own ticket.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (Customers book through NorthByte's website, its mobile app, corporate travel portals, or online travel agencies, and can pay by credit card, debit, travel voucher, or a combination of NorthByte Rewards points and cash. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (On top of the base fare, NorthByte earns ancillary revenue from optional extras:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
