503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 263 0 R
/E (Every flight NorthByte operates carries a cost, whether it departs full or nearly empty. NorthByte's finance team records four categories of operating cost for every flight it operates:)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1618 0 R
/E (Fuel: jet fuel burned on each flight. Longer routes burn significantly more fuel, and prices fluctuate with global oil markets. NorthByte's average fuel cost per flight rose by about 3% in FY2025-26 compared to FY2024-25.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1619 0 R
/E (Crew: wages and expenses for pilots and cabin crew. Following the new pilot agreement, NorthByte's average crew cost per flight rose by about 4% in FY2025-26.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1620 0 R
/E (Maintenance: scheduled inspections, repairs, and parts. Maintenance needs increase with the number of flights and are heavier in winter.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1621 0 R
/E (Food: catering loaded onto the aircraft, including complimentary snacks and drinks and items stocked for onboard sale.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
508 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 263 0 R
/E (Because most of these costs depend on the number of flights rather than the number of passengers, a flight with half its seats empty costs nearly as much to operate as a full one. NorthByte's finance team has historically reviewed costs at the company level, by category, rather than route by route.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [17]
>>
