/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 265 0 R
/T (In a country as large as Canada, air travel is more than a convenience. It connects families across provinces, moves business travellers between economic centres, and keeps smaller and northern communities linked to the rest of the country. Yet behind every boarding pass is one of the thinnest-margin businesses in the world: airlines spend heavily on fuel, crews, aircraft, and airport space long before a single passenger boards.)
/E (In a country as large as Canada, air travel is more than a convenience. It connects families across provinces, moves business travellers between economic centres, and keeps smaller and northern communities linked to the rest of the country. Yet behind every boarding pass is one of the thinnest-margin businesses in the world: airlines spend heavily on fuel, crews, aircraft, and airport space long before a single passenger boards.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
