/P 267 0 R
/E (NorthByte Airlines is growing, but it is not growing profitably. Revenue is at a record high, yet NorthByte now spends more to run its flights than it earns from them. Without a clear picture of where its money is being lost, NorthByte risks spending its limited budget on the wrong fix.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
678 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 267 0 R
/E (The challenge is to look past company-wide totals and understand where NorthByte actually makes and loses money. Many factors play a role, but not every factor matters equally. Any solution must also stay true to NorthByte's values: protecting safety, treating customers fairly, and continuing to connect communities across Canada, while returning the airline to a sustainable level of profit.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13]
>>
