1829 0 obj
<<
/Title (In a country as large as Canada, air travel is more than a convenience. It connects families across provinces, moves business travellers between economic centres, and keeps smaller and northern communities linked to the rest of the country. Yet behind every boarding pass is one of the thinnest-margin businesses in the world: airlines spend heavily on fuel, crews, aircraft, and airport space long before a single passenger boards.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 972 0 R
/Next 2284 0 R
>>
endobj
1830 0 obj
<<
/Title (NorthByte Airlines is a fully domestic carrier serving 20 airports across Canada, from Victoria to St. John's and as far north as Whitehorse and Yellowknife. Most flights connect through four major airports \(Vancouver, Calgary, Toronto, and Montreal\), while regional routes link smaller cities into the network.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 972 0 R
/Prev 2285 0 R
/First 2286 0 R
/Last 2287 0 R
/Count -3
>>
endobj
